{{!
    A purchase order is a document, not a record preview — DESIGN_DECISIONS §1.2, accepted
    by Ron. So this is a full-width route view rather than a right-hand panel. §E's
    must-never for the screen is putting the line-item grid in a 500px panel, which is
    exactly what the overlay did.

    Two component facts this template is built around, both checked rather than assumed:

    1. `details` used to be a child of `index`, whose template renders the table and then
       an outlet. An overlay floated above that; a full-width view would have rendered
       BELOW the entire list. It is a sibling of `index` now, at the same URL.

    2. Layout::Section::Header has NO @actionButtons argument — its only yield sits inside
       the actions wormhole, so buttons go in the block and nowhere else. Passing
       @actionButtons would have silently rendered nothing.
}}
<Layout::Container>
    <Layout::Section>
        <Layout::Section::Header @title={{@model.order_number}} @subtitle={{@model.supplier.name}} @status={{@model.status}}>
            {{#each this.actionButtons as |button|}}
                <Button @icon={{button.icon}} @type={{or button.type "default"}} @text={{button.text}} @helpText={{button.helpText}} @onClick={{button.fn}} @wrapperClass="ml-2" />
            {{/each}}
            <Button @icon="list" @type="default" @text={{t "purchase-order.actions.back-to-list"}} @onClick={{transition-to "orders.purchase-orders.index"}} @wrapperClass="ml-2" />
        </Layout::Section::Header>

        <Layout::Section::Body>
            {{! Renders details/index.hbs. The component is not inlined here or it would
                appear twice. }}
            <div class="space-y-3 p-4">
                {{outlet}}
            </div>
        </Layout::Section::Body>
    </Layout::Section>
</Layout::Container>